HIT POLICY rule_order: selected fired, either
[ ] both (not fired): (a > 1 OR b > 1) AND (c > 1 OR d > 1)
    would fire if all of these changed:
    - any of:
      - a > 1 is false (a = 0); short by 1
      - b > 1 is false (b = 0); short by 1
    - any of:
      - c > 1 is false (c = 0); short by 1
      - d > 1 is false (d = 0); short by 1
[x] fired (selected): (a < 1 OR b > 1) AND c < 1
    because all of these hold:
    - a < 1 is true (a = 0)
    - c < 1 is true (c = 0)
[x] either (selected): a < 1 OR b < 1
    because any of these hold:
    - a < 1 is true (a = 0)
    - b < 1 is true (b = 0)
[ ] conflict (not fired): a > 1 AND NOT a > 1
    cannot fire by changing these conditions alone; they conflict:
    - a > 1 is false (a = 0); short by 1
